===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|osp|conejo}}, from {{inh|es|VL.|cuniclus}}, syncopated form of {{inh|es|la|cunīculus}} originally "burrow", from {{der|es|grc|κύνικλος}}, of pre-Roman (probably {{der|es|xib|-}}) origin; compare {{cog|eu|untxi||rabbit}}. Compare {{cog|gl|coello}}, {{cog|pt|coelho}}, {{cog|ca|conill}}, and {{cog|oc|conilh}}.

